# JSONPath Exam Challenges

Try to solve each challenge using `kubectl` and `-o jsonpath` or `--sort-by` in under 60 seconds without consulting `solutions.md`.

> [!TIP]
> Permitted Exam Reference: [JSONPath Support](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/jsonpath/) | [kubectl Cheat Sheet - Formatting Output](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/cheatsheet/#formatting-output)

## Challenge 1: Node Internal IPs

Extract all node internal IPs separated by spaces.

- Target Output: e.g. `192.168.56.20 192.168.56.21 192.168.56.22`

## Challenge 2: Node Architecture and OS Images

Display each node's name, architecture, and OS image separated by tabs.

- Fields: `metadata.name`, `status.nodeInfo.architecture`, `status.nodeInfo.osImage`

## Challenge 3: kube-system Pod Names

Extract the name of every pod currently in the `kube-system` namespace, each on a new line.

## Challenge 4: Control Plane Component Images

Extract the image used by the `kube-apiserver` static pod in `kube-system`.

## Challenge 5: Pods Sorted by Creation Timestamp

List all pods in `kube-system` sorted chronologically by `metadata.creationTimestamp`.

## Challenge 6: Service Names and ClusterIPs

List all Services across all namespaces with format `NAME: <name>, CLUSTER-IP: <ip>`.

## Challenge 7: Find Non-Running Pods

Extract the names of any pods in the cluster whose `status.phase` is NOT equal to `Running`.

## Challenge 8: ConfigMap Keys

Extract all data keys contained in the `kube-root-ca.crt` ConfigMap in the `default` namespace.

## Challenge 9: PersistentVolume Capacities

Extract all PV names and their allocated storage capacity.

## Challenge 10: Node Capacity CPU and Memory

Extract each node's name, total CPU count, and allocatable memory.

- Fields: `status.capacity.cpu`, `status.allocatable.memory`
